for ax,color in zip(axes,('red','green','blue')):
 t,e=curves[color]
 for i,n in enumerate(('pan','lift','elbow','wrist flex','wrist roll','gripper')):ax.plot(t,e[:,i]*1000,label=n,lw=.8)
 ax.set_title(color+' executed-command replay');ax.set_ylabel('Joint error (mdeg)');ax.grid(alpha=.2)
axes[0].legend(ncol=3,fontsize=8);axes[-1].set_xlabel('Recorded action index /30 (sim s)');fig.tight_layout();fig.savefig(a.out/'executed-joint-errors.png',dpi=150);plt.close(fig)
lines=['READY for policy integration: the native held-tick path placed all six replays (3/3 clean labels and 3/3 recorded executed commands). Every command was applied at its observation tick with exact float32 native target read-back, followed by exactly one 30 Hz simulation frame. For the executed-command arm, pre-closure TCP RMS error was below 0.001 mm for every colour, without a timing shift. The GPU was released at 12:41:40Z with cleanup exit 0. This qualifies the actuation path; policy RPC/camera integration and policy scoring remain pending.','', '| Commands | Colour | Grasp / placement | Exact targets | Pre-close TCP RMS / max (mm) | Full TCP RMS / max (mm) |','|---|---|---|---:|---:|---:|']
for r in rows:lines.append(f"| {r['commands']} | {r['color']} | {int(r['grasp'])} / {int(r['success'])} | {r['target_readback_exact']}/{r['actions']} | {r['preclosure_tcp_rms_mm']:.6f} / {r['preclosure_tcp_max_mm']:.6f} | {r['full_tcp_rms_mm']:.6f} / {r['full_tcp_max_mm']:.6f} |")
lines+=['','Per-joint RMS and maximum absolute errors for all six joints are in replay-metrics.csv. These are action-index-aligned comparisons to the recorded measured state, without any fitted lag. Clean labels differ from the commands actually applied during training by up to 0.92–0.99 degrees because of DART; clean-label red/blue trajectory differences therefore do not imply an actuation error. The executed-command arm is the direct trajectory reproduction test.','', 'The adapter imports the unchanged collector command/ACK, native apply/advance, sensor join and ownership code from exact collection cut bf7336d. All eleven core files are byte-compared with that cut and their hashes appear in the raw receipts. Only a private rtx6000 worktree is used. Domain92 uses SHA-pinned loopback CycloneDDS; the runtime independently verifies the active GPU UUID/PCI mapping. No model ran. Reset restores recorded joint state, drive targets and body poses, zeros velocities, and advances one unrecorded bootstrap frame after the reset floor. Those reset differences limit bit-exact initial-state reproduction and are recorded.','', 'Small N: 3/3 has a 95% Wilson interval of 43.9–100%; this is an actuation acceptance test on expert actions, not an estimate of model success or generalisation. Source, raw compressed traces, CPU checks, independent code review and window START/STOP receipts are provided. Independent raw outcome/metric review is pending.','', 'Two startup attempts ended before any replay episode: a new runtime first lacked the required prior owned Kit GPU table, then the sourced Humble environment reintroduced ROS_LOCALHOST_ONLY=0 and failed the explicit isolation guard. Both attempts stopped with cleanup0. A provenance-recorded prior owned table supplied the launcher hint; the fresh launch then verified the current renderer. The child now unsets the three discovery variables after sourcing and checks them through the same CPU-tested guard function. The completed window is native-held-replay-v3.']
(a.out/'README.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n');print('\n'.join(lines[:10]));shutil.copy2(a.archive,a.out/a.archive.name)
